# Prototype the Page Annotation UI

## Step

The earliest touchable artifact: annotation on one real rendered Brain page. Select text, write a comment, submit — the prototype writes a real receipt file locally (no gateway, no commit plumbing, throwaway endpoint is fine). Run via the `prototype` skill.

Constraints from the brief's Notes:

- **Phone-first**: Joel reviews it on his phone over the tailnet; if selection and typing are clumsy there, the prototype has done its job by failing loudly.
- One real page from a registered root, rendered by the live renderer — not a mock document.
- The receipt it writes should be a plausible draft of the contract (page, commit, span, text), so the prototype feeds the receipt-contract grilling a concrete strawman rather than waiting on it.

Deliberately not blocked on the write-path or receipt-contract grillings — a reaction to a touchable thing is input to those decisions, not downstream of them.

Resolved when Joel has annotated a real page from his phone and his reactions (UX, selection model, what felt missing) are recorded here for the write-path and receipt-contract grillings to consume.
